APEX ACADEMIC UNIVERSITY
Official Policy: Graduate Assistantship & Tuition
Remission Regulations
DOCUMENT TITLE: Graduate Assistantship and Research Regulations
DOCUMENT TYPE: faculty_policy
EFFECTIVE DATE: Fall Semester 2025
VERSION: 4.2
SECTION 1: GRADUATE ASSISTANTSHIP ELIGIBILITY & WORKLOAD
1.1 Graduate Teaching Assistants (GTAs) and Graduate Research Assistants (GRAs) must maintain full-time
enrollment of at least 9 credit hours per semester during the academic year.
1.2 The maximum allowable appointment workload for a Graduate Assistant is 20 hours per week during
regular Fall and Spring semesters. Overtime beyond 20 hours requires prior written authorization from the
Graduate Dean.
1.3 Graduate Assistants must maintain a minimum Cumulative GPA of 3.25. If the CGPA drops below 3.25, the
assistantship is placed on conditional probation for one semester.
SECTION 2: STIPEND RATES AND TUITION REMISSION
2.1 Full-time 20-hour Graduate Assistantships include a minimum monthly stipend of $2,200 plus 100% full
tuition remission for up to 12 graduate credit hours per semester.
2.2 University mandatory student fees (health fee, technology fee, activity fee) are not covered by tuition
remission and remain the personal financial responsibility of the student.
2.3 Tuition remission benefits are applied to the student financial account within 10 business days following the
formal execution of the Assistantship Contract.
SECTION 3: LEAVE POLICIES AND TERMINATION CONDITIONS
3.1 Graduate Assistants are entitled to 5 paid leave business days per semester for personal illness or family
emergencies, subject to approval by the Faculty Advisor.
3.2 Assistantship contracts may be terminated immediately for cause in cases of gross neglect of duty, violation
of university code of conduct, or academic misconduct.